{
  "note": "Canonical i18n ADDRESSES — the cross-language contract of inline mode. A document holds the default language's literal text; every other language sits in lang/<lang>.yaml at the address of its key site. The editor mints those addresses when it writes the lang files (domain/i18nSites.ts + lib/i18nKeys.ts); the plugin re-derives them from the file structure when it reads them (engine/I18nAddresses.kt, MenuTitleParser, DialogTextResolver). Disagree on one address and a translation lands where the runtime never looks. Owned by: editor/src/features/export/i18nAddressConformance.test.ts + plugin I18nAddressConformanceTest.kt — changing the scheme means updating both and this file. Action texts (`step_addresses`): a case gives either a legacy `dsl` chain or keyed `steps` (the structured wire, module actions included), plus the `declared_actions` of the module actions it uses, in the Presence wire shape. The rule is driven by each action's schema: an ltext argument with a legacy slot (send_message/broadcast → message, show_title → show_title/show_subtitle) counts per slot; any other ltext argument hangs off the action's name (`:` read as `.`), numbered per occurrence of that action, a list(ltext) numbering its entries _2, _3…; an absent optional text consumes nothing; an undeclared action has no text site.",

  "sites": [
